flowchart TB
    accTitle: The first host-bounded response loop
    accDescr: Before requesting each fake model response, the host compares the response count with the maximum. If the allowance is exhausted, it returns a budget terminal result without another request. Otherwise it reads one response and increments the count. A final response terminates; an observe response appends its observation and returns to the allowance check.
    G("Below response cap?")
    G -->|"No"| X["Stop: response cap"]
    G -->|"Yes"| M["Read one FakeModel response"]
    M --> C["Increment response count"]
    C --> K("Response kind?")
    K -->|"final"| F["Stop: final answer"]
    K -->|"observe"| O["Append observation"]
    O --> G
